    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0357" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Sm 61/185: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Hungary</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-24T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1922—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 25, 10:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Letter accrediting me as Chargé d’Affaires erroneously refers to “Republic of
                    Hungary”. Minister for Foreign Affairs has consented to accept it provisionally
                    until the receipt of letter referring to “Kingdom of Hungary”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
